    "description": "CCCC MS 640, a single leaf from a Spanish sixteenth-century Antiphoner, was given to the Parker Library by Andrew Johnson in 2008. The text is from First Vespers and Matins of the Seventh Sunday after Pentecost. There are large calligraphic initials tinted in pale yellow for the responsory and versicle."
  },
